'''Cedric Darryl Pollard''' (born May 11, 1964) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[cornerback]] for seven seasons in the [[National Football League]] (NFL). His listed highlights{{according to whom|date=February 2016}} are the [[Super Bowl XXIII]] and [[Super Bowl XXIV|XXIV]] championships, and playing on an undefeated Colorado State High School Championship team in 1981.{{citation needed|date=February 2016}}

