'''Darryl Gerard Lewis''' (born April 16, 1961) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] [[tight end]] who played one season with the [[Cleveland Browns]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL).<ref>{{cite book|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ZHFVAwAAQBAJ&q=Darryl+Lewis+browns+1984&pg=PA71 |title=Uniform Numbers of the NFL: All-Time Rosters, Facts and Figures |publisher=McFarland |author=Maxymuk, John |year=2005 |pages=71 |isbn=9780786420575 |url-status=bot: unknown |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160813234440/https://books.google.com/books?id=ZHFVAwAAQBAJ&pg=PA71&lpg=PA71&dq=Darryl+Lewis+browns+1984&source=bl&ots=SlIOkzzrEi&sig=NjJeDXFu0xLiH16nCj8IeYhN-so&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiX_tjzyL_OAhVHSyYKHShGDosQ6AEIUjAL#v=onepage&q=Darryl |archivedate=August 13, 2016 }}</ref> He was selected by the [[New England Patriots]] in the fifth round of the [[1983 NFL draft]]. He played [[college football]] at the [[University of Texas at Arlington]] and attended [[Daingerfield High School]] in [[Daingerfield, Texas]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.profootballarchives.com/lewi01800.html | title=DARRYL LEWIS | publisher=profootballarchives.com | accessdate=August 13, 2016 | archive-date=August 13, 2016 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160813232837/http://www.profootballarchives.com/lewi01800.html | url-status=dead }}</ref> Lewis's brother, [[Gary Lewis (tight end)|Gary]], also played in the NFL.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/L/LewiDa21.htm | title=Darryl Lewis | publisher=Sports Reference LLC | work=pro-football-reference.com | accessdate=August 13, 2016}}</ref>
